    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1995670808862359834",
      "url": "https://x.com/marortoll/status/1995670808862359834",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/marortoll/status/1995670808862359834",
      "text": "The truth is no political bloc can; provide a viable endgame that is. \n\nIn Erap's case, the denouement was the impeachment trial. The manufactured evidence and the existence of the Jose Velarde account provided the trigger. Along with the houses Erap was building for each of his mistresses, these convinced the middle class that Erap was guilty. It was the catalyst for Edsa 2 which ousted him and it also helped that the GMA camp had a ready plan supported by both Cory and FVR which led to the final withdrawal of support for the Erap administration. \n\nIn this case, there is none. While the administration is on the defensive, it is by no measure of the administration, on the verge of being overthrown or ousted. \n\nSince its six year term is now a foregone conclusion, what comes next is continuing political instability. \n\nThe Reds, together with the administration, will go after Inday with impeachment and criminal charges. The vice-president is not immune from suit. \n\nShould Inday continue to dominate the presidential race in 2028, there is the chance that the administration could see its congressional majority weaken and enable the impeachment of the president. \n\nWhile this scenario is a probability, its coming to a fruition is low considering how greedy our legislators are. They can be bribed with campaign funds for the 2028 election. \n\nLong story short, we're stuck with waiting for the 2028 election. How the administration will fare depends largely on its handling of the flood control scam. It rests on the public being satisfied with whoever big fish is served up on a silver platter. \n\nThe supreme court ruling about fugitives not being entitled to judicial relief will have a major impact because they are not allowed to participate in court proceedings by their counsels. \n\nTheir ability and financial wherewithal to be on the run are keys to their survival. \n\nBut who knows? \n\nZaldy Co may still have a bombshell revelation. What happens next depends on what the principal players decide. Whether we care to admit it or not, we the people are just pawns in the games our leaders play. \n\nSo much for democracy. \n\n\"Those who claim leadership over the anti-corruption protest movement must take responsibility for the tepid public response. Neither of the two wings of the protest movement offers a viable strategy and a convincing endgame for the largest corruption scandal in our country’s history.\"\nhttps://t.co/ALLohlfbyo",
